    "description": "Eco Park (প্রকৃতি তীর্থ) is an urban park in New Town, Kolkata, India. With an area of 190 hectares (480 acres), including a 42 hectares (104 acres) waterbody, Eco Park is the largest urban park in India. The park was conceptualised by Mamata Banerjee, the CM of West Bengal, in July 2011. It is constructed under the oversight of WBHIDCO, along with different other government bodies responsible for implementation of different works inside the park.",
